        description: Sidebar nav row. Active state uses brand primary as a left-edge indicator bar.
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.canvas}"
        activeIndicator: "{tokens.color.primary}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.sm}"
        padding: "{tokens.spacing.xs} {tokens.spacing.sm}"
  ex-data-table-cell:
    description: "DESIGN.md component token group"
    when: ["as documented in rationale.components and getdesign analysis"]
    when_not: ["decorative misuse outside brand patterns"]
    variants: [default]
    tokens:
      default:
        description: Mirrors the brand's table chrome. Header uses caption-mono uppercase mono; body uses body-sm.
        headerBackground: "{tokens.color.canvas-soft}"
        headerTypography: "{tokens.typography.caption-mono}"
        bodyTypography: "{tokens.typography.body-sm}"
        cellPadding: "{tokens.spacing.xs} {tokens.spacing.sm}"
        rowBorder: "{tokens.color.hairline}"
  ex-auth-form-card:
    description: "DESIGN.md component token group"
    when: ["as documented in rationale.components and getdesign analysis"]
    when_not: ["decorative misuse outside brand patterns"]
    variants: [default]
    tokens:
      default:
        description: Sign-in / sign-up card. Mirrors card-marketing-large chrome with form-input primitives inside.
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.canvas-soft}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.lg}"
        padding: "{tokens.spacing.xl}"
  ex-modal-card:
    description: "DESIGN.md component token group"
    when: ["as documented in rationale.components and getdesign analysis"]
    when_not: ["decorative misuse outside brand patterns"]
    variants: [default]
    tokens:
      default:
        description: Modal dialog surface — same chrome as card-marketing-large with Level 5 modal shadow.
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.canvas}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.lg}"
        padding: "{tokens.spacing.xl}"
  ex-empty-state-card:
    description: "DESIGN.md component token group"
    when: ["as documented in rationale.components and getdesign analysis"]
    when_not: ["decorative misuse outside brand patterns"]
    variants: [default]
    tokens:
      default:
        description: Empty-state illustration frame. Generous padding on canvas-soft.
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.canvas-soft}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.lg}"
        padding: "{tokens.spacing.3xl}"
        captionTypography: "{tokens.typography.body-md}"
  ex-toast:
    description: "DESIGN.md component token group"
    when: ["as documented in rationale.components and getdesign analysis"]
    when_not: ["decorative misuse outside brand patterns"]
    variants: [default]
    tokens:
      default:
        description: Toast notification surface — flat-cornered card-marketing chrome with Level 4 shadow.
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.canvas}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.md}"
        padding: "{tokens.spacing.sm} {tokens.spacing.md}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.body-sm}"

rationale:
  overview: |
    Vercel is a developer-platform brand — the page is a deployment dashboard's marketing surface, written for engineers who already know the syntax. It earns that posture with one of the cleanest stark systems on the web: near-white `{tokens.color.canvas-soft}` body background, ink-near-black `{tokens.color.ink}` text, a 200-step gray scale that gives every divider, border, and disabled state its own deliberate step. The only place the brand introduces colour at marketing scale is the multi-stop mesh gradient (`{tokens.color.gradient-develop-start}` → `{tokens.color.gradient-preview-end}` → `{tokens.color.gradient-ship-start}` → cyan / magenta / amber) that floats in atmospheric backdrops, never miniaturised to a swatch. That gradient is the entire decoration system.
    
    Type is the second decisive voice. The brand's own custom geometric sans (Geist) carries display, body, button — everything narrative — at weight 600 for display, 500 for buttons, 400 for body. A matching monospaced face (Geist Mono) carries technical labels: terminal mockups, code blocks, sometimes filename captions. Headlines are sentence-case with aggressive negative letter-spacing (`-2.4px` at 48 px hero) — the brand never letter-spaces positively, never goes uppercase outside of mono labels.
    
    Surfaces use a four-step ladder: `{tokens.color.canvas}` (pure white for cards), `{tokens.color.canvas-soft}` 98% (the page body), `{tokens.color.canvas-soft-2}` 95% (occasional inset region), `{tokens.color.primary}` (the deep ink-near-black used as the polarity-flipped band when a section needs the dark mode treatment). Shadows are exceptionally subtle — every elevated card carries a stacked shadow built from `0px 1px 1px #00000005` + `0px 2px 2px #0000000a` + an inset border. Cards never float on heavy drop-shadow; they sit on the page held by hairline + soft glow.
    
    **Key Characteristics:**
    - A single black-ink primary CTA `{tokens.color.primary}` carries every conversion target, paired with white-on-white `button-secondary` for the secondary action. The brand uses 100 px pill shape for marketing CTAs and a tight 6 px square shape for in-app nav buttons.
    - A multi-stop mesh gradient (cyan-blue-magenta-amber) is the only decorative chrome — used at hero scale and inside feature-band atmospheric backdrops. It is the brand.
    - Every section eyebrow and small label uses the monospace face `{tokens.typography.caption-mono}` or `{tokens.typography.code}`; everything else is in the geometric sans.
    - Subtle stacked-shadow elevation — three offsets layered with 4-12 % black opacity — never a single heavy drop-shadow.
    - A complete 100–1000 gray + blue + red + amber + green + teal + purple + pink colour scale exists as a system token set, but the marketing surface uses only the `100`, `1000`, and `700`-level tones; the rest stay in the design-system tokens for in-product surfaces.
    - An "Active CPU" pricing rhythm: `pricing-card` lays out 3-up on the pricing page with `pricing-card-featured` (Pro tier) polarity-flipped to `{tokens.color.primary}` against white-card siblings.
  colors: |
    ### Brand & Accent
    - **Ink** (`{tokens.color.primary}` — `#171717`): The single primary CTA color. Black-near-pure ink that carries every Sign Up pill, every footer CTA, the dark-band polarity-flip. Used as text color throughout the page on light surfaces. (Resolved from `--ds-gray-1000`.)
    - **Cyan** (`{tokens.color.cyan}` — `#50e3c2`): A signature mint-cyan used in the brand gradient and inside Geist-system spotlight tokens. Visible inside the hero gradient stops.
    - **Highlight Pink** (`{tokens.color.highlight-pink}` — `#ff0080`): The brand's highlight magenta, used as the high-saturation stop in the preview-gradient pair.
    - **Violet** (`{tokens.color.violet}` — `#7928ca`): The deep purple used as the start of the preview-gradient and inside developer-console highlights.
    - **Link Blue** (`{tokens.color.link}` — `#0070f3`): The brand's primary link color and the legacy `--geist-success` semantic.
    
    ### Surface
    - **Canvas** (`{tokens.color.canvas}` — `#ffffff`): The pure-white card / dialog / modal surface.
    - **Canvas Soft** (`{tokens.color.canvas-soft}` — `#fafafa`): The default page background — 98 % white. Almost every section sits on this tone.
    - **Canvas Soft 2** (`{tokens.color.canvas-soft-2}` — `#f5f5f5`): A slightly deeper inset surface for "code editor inner background", template-card hover states, and dropdown menus.
    - **Hairline** (`{tokens.color.hairline}` — `#ebebeb`): 1 px dividers — table rows, card borders, input borders.
    - **Hairline Strong** (`{tokens.color.hairline-strong}` — `#a1a1a1`): The 500-level gray, used as the slightly-stronger divider on light bands and as the deemphasised text color.
    
    ### Text
    - **Ink** (`{tokens.color.ink}` — `#171717`): Every heading and body paragraph on light surfaces.
    - **Body** (`{tokens.color.body}` — `#4d4d4d`): Secondary text — sub-headings, body captions, nav-link inactive text, footer column body.
    - **Mute** (`{tokens.color.mute}` — `#888888`): Lowest-priority text — placeholder text, fine print, low-key labels.
    - **On Primary** (`{tokens.color.on-primary}` — `#ffffff`): All text on `{tokens.color.primary}` surfaces.
    
    ### Semantic
    - **Success / Link** (`{tokens.color.success}` — `#0070f3`): The brand's legacy success indicator doubles as the primary link color. Visible underline-on-hover for inline body links.
    - **Link Deep** (`{tokens.color.link-deep}` — `#0761d1`): The pressed / visited tone for inline links.
    - **Link Bg Soft** (`{tokens.color.link-bg-soft}` — `#d3e5ff`): Soft pastel blue fill for "what's new" pill banners and informational badges.
    - **Error** (`{tokens.color.error}` — `#ee0000`): Validation red for destructive actions and form errors.
    - **Error Soft** (`{tokens.color.error-soft}` — `#f7d4d6`): Soft pastel red for destructive-state backgrounds.
    - **Error Deep** (`{tokens.color.error-deep}` — `#c50000`): Pressed / deep destructive state.
    - **Warning** (`{tokens.color.warning}` — `#f5a623`): Caution / pending status indicator.
    - **Warning Soft** (`{tokens.color.warning-soft}` — `#ffefcf`) / **Warning Deep** (`{tokens.color.warning-deep}` — `#ab570a`): Background + pressed variants.
    
    ### Brand Gradient
    The brand's signature decoration is a three-pair gradient stack:
    - **Develop** (`{tokens.color.gradient-develop-start}` `#007cf0` → `{tokens.color.gradient-develop-end}` `#00dfd8`) — the blue-to-teal pair used to mark the "deploy" / "develop" rhythm.
    - **Preview** (`{tokens.color.gradient-preview-start}` `#7928ca` → `{tokens.color.gradient-preview-end}` `#ff0080`) — the violet-to-pink pair used for "preview" surfaces.
    - **Ship** (`{tokens.color.gradient-ship-start}` `#ff4d4d` → `{tokens.color.gradient-ship-end}` `#f9cb28`) — the coral-to-amber pair used for "ship" surfaces.
    
    The three pairs collapse into a single multi-color mesh gradient when used as the hero atmospheric backdrop. Treat the gradient as one unified object — do not crop down to a single colour, do not reorder the stops, and do not miniaturise. Used at hero scale only.
  typography: |
    ### Font Family
    Two custom faces carry the entire system:
    
    1. **A custom geometric sans** (extracted as `Geist`) for every display, body, button, link, and label. Weights 400 / 500 / 600 are the working set; the face never appears in 700 or heavier. Display sizes are tracked aggressively negative (`-2.4 px` at 48 px hero, `-1.28 px` at 32 px section); body stays at neutral or slightly-negative tracking.
    2. **A custom monospaced face** (extracted as `Geist Mono`) for terminal mockups, code blocks, and small mono-caption labels — anything that wants to signal "technical." Weight 400 only at 12 – 13 px. Tracking neutral.
    
    A condensed display sans (`Space Grotesk`) is loaded as a third face for occasional editorial moments but does not render as the primary face anywhere in the captured surfaces.
    
    ### Hierarchy
    
    | Token | Size | Weight | Line Height | Letter Spacing | Use |
    |---|---|---|---|---|---|
    | `{tokens.typography.display-xl}` | 48px | 600 | 48px | -2.4px | Hero headline ("Build and deploy on the AI Cloud."). |
    | `{tokens.typography.display-lg}` | 32px | 600 | 40px | -1.28px | Section headlines ("Your frontend, delivered.", "A compute model for all workloads."). |
    | `{tokens.typography.display-md}` | 24px | 600 | 32px | -0.96px | Card-cluster headlines, pricing-tier names. |
    | `{tokens.typography.display-sm}` | 20px | 600 | 28px | -0.6px | Inline display micro-headings. |
    | `{tokens.typography.body-lg}` | 18px | 400 | 28px | 0 | Lead paragraphs under section headlines. |
    | `{tokens.typography.body-md}` | 16px | 400 | 24px | 0 | Default body paragraph. |
    | `{tokens.typography.body-md-strong}` | 16px | 500 | 24px | 0 | Bolded inline body. |
    | `{tokens.typography.body-sm}` | 14px | 400 | 20px | -0.28px | Secondary body, nav-link text, button-md labels. |
    | `{tokens.typography.body-sm-strong}` | 14px | 500 | 20px | -0.28px | Nav CTA labels, table-row emphasis. |
    | `{tokens.typography.caption}` | 12px | 400 | 16px | 0 | Footer secondary lines, badge labels. |
    | `{tokens.typography.caption-mono}` | 12px | 400 | 16px | 0 | Section eyebrows and label captions that want a technical voice. |
    | `{tokens.typography.code}` | 13px | 400 | 20px | 0 | Inline code, terminal mockups, command snippets. |
    | `{tokens.typography.button-md}` | 14px | 500 | 20px | 0 | Small / nav-scale button labels. |
    | `{tokens.typography.button-lg}` | 16px | 500 | 24px | 0 | Marketing-scale pill button labels. |
    
    ### Principles
    - **Negative tracking is part of the voice.** Display sizes use aggressive `-2.4` to `-0.6` px tracking. Reverting to default tracking breaks the brand.
    - **Sentence-case headlines, period-terminated.** Headlines like "Build and deploy on the AI Cloud." end with a deliberate period — that punctuation is part of the brand's voice.
    - **Mono for the technical layer only.** Section eyebrows, code blocks, terminal mockups. Body paragraphs never set in mono.
    - **Weight 600 is the display ceiling.** The geometric sans never appears at 700 / 800. The brand reads as a calmer system because of this.
    
    ### Note on Font Substitutes
    The two primary faces are proprietary (custom-cut for the brand). Open-source substitutes:
    - **Geometric sans** — *Inter* (400 / 500 / 600) is the closest stylistic match; `font-feature-settings: "ss01", "ss02"` enables the geometric alternates. *Satoshi* is a passable second choice.
    - **Monospace** — *JetBrains Mono* (400) at 12 – 13 px matches the technical voice. *IBM Plex Mono* is the second-best option.
  layout: |
    ### Spacing System
    - **Base unit**: 4 px. The brand's `--geist-space` token is exactly 4 px and every captured value is a multiple of 4.
    - **Tokens**: `{tokens.spacing.xxs}` 4 px · `{tokens.spacing.xs}` 8 px · `{tokens.spacing.sm}` 12 px · `{tokens.spacing.md}` 16 px · `{tokens.spacing.lg}` 24 px · `{tokens.spacing.xl}` 32 px · `{tokens.spacing.2xl}` 40 px · `{tokens.spacing.3xl}` 48 px · `{tokens.spacing.4xl}` 64 px · `{tokens.spacing.5xl}` 96 px · `{tokens.spacing.6xl}` 128 px · `{tokens.spacing.section}` 192 px.
    - **Section padding**: marketing bands use `{tokens.spacing.4xl}` to `{tokens.spacing.5xl}` top/bottom. Hero bands stretch to `{tokens.spacing.section}` to give the mesh gradient room to breathe.
    - **Card interior padding**: marketing cards sit at `{tokens.spacing.lg}` to `{tokens.spacing.xl}`; template-grid cards stay tighter at `{tokens.spacing.md}` because they sit in a denser grid.
    - **Inline gap**: button rows, nav rows, and chip rows use `{tokens.spacing.sm}` to `{tokens.spacing.md}` between siblings. The brand's `--geist-gap` is exactly 24 px.
    
    ### Grid & Container
    - **Max width**: ~1400 px (`--ds-page-width`); the legacy `--geist-page-width` is 1200 px and still appears on some marketing surfaces. Content centres with horizontal gutters of `{tokens.spacing.lg}` 24 px on desktop, `{tokens.spacing.md}` 16 px on mobile.
    - **Column patterns**:
      - Three-feature row: 3-up at desktop, 1-up at mobile (rows like "Web Apps / Composable Commerce / Multi-tenant Platforms").
      - Tab pill row: 5-up centred row of `tab-ghost` pills.
      - Template-grid cluster: 5-up at desktop, scaling to 1-up at mobile.
      - Pricing tier grid: 3-up at desktop with the middle tier polarity-flipped.
      - Logo strip: ~5 logos wide, single row.
    
    ### Whitespace Philosophy
    The mesh gradient does most of the heavy decorative lifting; whitespace separates the bands. Section spacing is generous — `{tokens.spacing.4xl}` to `{tokens.spacing.5xl}` between bands lets the gradient breathe. Inside a card, the headline/paragraph stack is tight (`{tokens.spacing.xs}` 8 px gap), then a wider gap before the CTA cluster. The page reads as engineered — large gaps + tight interior, never the other way around.
    
    ### Responsive Strategy
    
    #### Breakpoints
    
    | Name | Width | Key Changes |
    |---|---|---|
    | Mobile | < 600px | Hero stacks; nav collapses to hamburger; 3-up feature grids drop to 1-up; tab pill row enables horizontal scroll. |
    | Tablet | 600–959px | 3-up grids drop to 2-up; nav still horizontal. |
    | Desktop | 960–1199px | Full 3-up grids; pricing 3-up. |
    | Wide | 1200–1399px | Container caps at 1400 px content width. |
    | Ultra-wide | ≥ 1400px | Content stays centred at 1400 px; bands stretch edge-to-edge in colour but content holds the max-width. |
    
    #### Touch Targets
    The `button-primary` pill renders at ~32 px tall in nav and ~48 px tall in marketing contexts. Marketing CTAs comfortably meet WCAG AAA at all breakpoints; nav buttons inflate touch area through `{tokens.spacing.xs}` padding on mobile to meet the 44 × 44 px floor.
    
    #### Collapsing Strategy
    - **Nav**: full link row + Ask AI / Log In / Sign Up pills at desktop. Collapses to logo + hamburger at mobile with the menu opening as a full-overlay.
    - **Hero**: mesh gradient stays centred; headline + body stack vertically at all breakpoints (the brand doesn't use a split-hero pattern).
    - **Three-feature row**: 3-up → 2-up → 1-up at the breakpoints above; cards keep their `{tokens.radius.md}` 8 px shape across all viewports.
    - **Pricing card grid**: 3-up at desktop, vertical stack at mobile with `pricing-card-featured` always sitting in the middle.
    - **Template grid**: 5-up → 3-up → 2-up → 1-up. Each `template-card` keeps its 16:9 aspect on the image.
    
    #### Image Behavior
    - **Mesh gradient**: rendered as inline SVG or canvas-painted gradient; scales fluidly with the hero container; never crops, never tiles.
    - **Customer logos**: rendered as monochrome SVGs in the logo strip; consistent 24 px height.
    - **Code editor mockup**: dark `{tokens.color.primary}` rectangle with mono text rendered inside; treated as an image at the layout level.
    - **Template thumbnails**: 16:9 landscape inside `{tokens.radius.md}` card chrome; lazy-loaded; consistent grayscale palette in the placeholder state.
  elevation: |
    | Level | Treatment | Use |
    |---|---|---|
    | Level 0 — Flat | No shadow, no border. | Full-bleed hero bands and the polarity-flipped dark sections. |
    | Level 1 — Inset Hairline | `0 0 0 1px #00000014` inset 1 px border. | Default card chrome — the brand's universal "you can see this card" cue. |
    | Level 2 — Subtle Drop | `0px 1px 1px #00000005, 0px 2px 2px #0000000a` plus inset hairline. | Slightly elevated cards (template-grid, marketing-card). |
    | Level 3 — Soft Stack | `0px 2px 2px #0000000a, 0px 8px 8px -8px #0000000a` plus inset hairline. | The "medium" elevation — feature-grid cards. |
    | Level 4 — Float Stack | `0px 2px 2px #0000000a, 0px 8px 16px -4px #0000000a` plus inset hairline. | "Large" elevation — pricing cards, callout panels. |
    | Level 5 — Modal | `0px 1px 1px #00000005, 0px 8px 16px -4px #0000000a, 0px 24px 32px -8px #0000000f` plus inset hairline. | Modal / dialog surfaces and dropdown menus. |
    
    The brand uses STACKED shadows — multiple small offsets layered to fake natural light — never a single 8-px-blur generic drop. Inset hairline rings are always added so the card edge stays crisp.
    
    ### Decorative Depth
    - **Mesh gradient as atmospheric depth**: the hero's multi-stop gradient is the brand's only "atmospheric" effect — applied as a flat 2-D backdrop rather than a 3-D illustration.
    - **Polarity-flipped dark band as section-depth**: switching the surface from `{tokens.color.canvas-soft}` to `{tokens.color.primary}` (the deep ink) is the brand's chief depth cue between bands.
    - **Inset-shadow + drop-shadow combo**: the cards' combination of an inset 1 px ring and a multi-stop drop produces a "card sits on the page" effect without ever feeling material-heavy.
  shapes: |
    ### Border Radius Scale
    
    | Token | Value | Use |
    |---|---|---|
    | `{tokens.radius.none}` | 0px | Full-bleed hero / footer bands. |
    | `{tokens.radius.xs}` | 4px | Tightest inline pill — the `nav-cta-signup` 6-px-radius button (mapped to `xs/sm`). |
    | `{tokens.radius.sm}` | 6px | The brand's `--geist-radius` token — base UI radius for in-app buttons, form inputs, dropdown menus. |
    | `{tokens.radius.md}` | 8px | The brand's `--geist-marketing-radius` token — feature cards, template cards. |
    | `{tokens.radius.lg}` | 12px | Slightly larger card chrome (pricing-card variants). |
    | `{tokens.radius.xl}` | 16px | Largest card chrome — when a card hosts a hero image cap. |
    | `{tokens.radius.pill-sm}` | 64px | Tab-ghost pills inside the "AI Apps / Web Apps / Ecommerce / Marketing / Platforms" row. |
    | `{tokens.radius.pill}` | 100px | The marketing CTA pill — `button-primary`, `button-secondary`, "Start Deploying" pill. |
    | `{tokens.radius.full}` | 9999px | Icon-button circular containers, nav-link ghost pills. |
    
    ### Photography Geometry
    - **Mesh gradient**: full-bleed 2-D atmospheric backdrop, never cropped to a frame; treated as the page's wallpaper.
    - **Customer logos**: monochrome SVG, consistent 24 px height in a flex row.
    - **Code editor mockup**: 16:10 dark rectangle, `{tokens.radius.md}` corners.
    - **Template thumbnails**: 16:9 landscape inside `{tokens.radius.md}` chrome.
    - **Showcase imagery**: 2:1 or 16:9 inside `{tokens.radius.lg}` to `{tokens.radius.xl}` chrome with a stacked shadow.
  components: |
    ### Buttons
    
    **`button-primary`** — the canonical 100-px-radius black pill, marketing scale.
    - Background `{tokens.color.primary}`, text `{tokens.color.on-primary}`, label set in `{tokens.typography.button-lg}`, padding `0px {tokens.spacing.sm}` 12 px, shape `{tokens.radius.pill}` 100 px. Renders ~48 px tall when paired with the marketing flex layout.
    
    **`button-secondary`** — the white pill paired with the black primary inside marketing bands.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, text `{tokens.color.ink}`, same typography + padding as `button-primary`, shape `{tokens.radius.pill}`.
    
    **`button-primary-sm`** — the smaller-scale primary pill used inside nav and pricing-card CTAs.
    - Background `{tokens.color.primary}`, text `{tokens.color.on-primary}`, label set in `{tokens.typography.button-md}` (14 px / 500), shape `{tokens.radius.pill}`.
    
    **`button-secondary-sm`** — the smaller-scale white pill paired with `button-primary-sm`.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, text `{tokens.color.ink}`, same typography + shape as `button-primary-sm`.
    
    **`tab-ghost`** — the centred-row tab pill ("AI Apps / Web Apps / Ecommerce / Marketing / Platforms").
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, text `{tokens.color.ink}`, label set in `{tokens.typography.body-sm}`, padding `0px {tokens.spacing.md}`, shape `{tokens.radius.pill-sm}` 64 px.
    
    **`icon-button-circular`** — the circular icon container (often a "?" or arrow inside).
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, dark icon, 1 px solid hairline border, shape `{tokens.radius.full}`.
    
    **Nav CTAs:**
    
    **`nav-cta-signup`** — the small black "Sign Up" button in the nav row.
    - Background `{tokens.color.primary}`, text `{tokens.color.on-primary}`, label `{tokens.typography.body-sm-strong}`, padding `0px {tokens.spacing.xs}`, height 28 px, shape `{tokens.radius.sm}` 6 px (the brand's `--geist-radius`).
    
    **`nav-cta-login`** — the white "Log In" button in the nav.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, text `{tokens.color.ink}`, same typography / height / shape as `nav-cta-signup`.
    
    **`nav-cta-ask-ai`** — the small "Ask AI" button with a faint border.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, text `{tokens.color.ink}`, 1 px solid `{tokens.color.hairline}` border (extracted as `0px solid rgb(235, 235, 235)`), same typography / height / shape.
    
    ### Cards & Containers
    
    **`card-marketing`** — the canonical marketing feature card (3-up section cards).
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, text `{tokens.color.ink}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.lg}` 24 px, shape `{tokens.radius.md}` 8 px (the `--geist-marketing-radius`). Carries Level 3 soft-stack shadow.
    
    **`card-marketing-large`** — the larger marketing card used for "compute model" / "AI Gateway" callouts.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, text `{tokens.color.ink}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.xl}`, shape `{tokens.radius.lg}` 12 px. Carries Level 4 float-stack shadow.
    
    **`card-soft`** — the soft-tinted card used inside cluster groups (lighter than canvas-soft).
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas-soft}`, text `{tokens.color.ink}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.lg}`, shape `{tokens.radius.md}`.
    
    **`template-card`** — the deploy-template card in the "Deploy your first app" grid.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, text `{tokens.color.ink}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.md}` 16 px, shape `{tokens.radius.md}` 8 px. Hosts a 16:9 thumbnail at the top.
    
    **`code-editor-mockup`** — the dark code-preview surface inside marketing bands.
    - Background `{tokens.color.primary}`, text `{tokens.color.on-primary}`, body in `{tokens.typography.code}` (13 px / Geist Mono), padding `{tokens.spacing.lg}` 24 px, shape `{tokens.radius.md}` 8 px.
    
    **`pricing-card`** — the default pricing-tier card.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, text `{tokens.color.ink}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.xl}` 32 px, shape `{tokens.radius.lg}` 12 px. Inside: tier name in `{tokens.typography.display-md}`, price in `{tokens.typography.display-xl}`, feature list in `{tokens.typography.body-md}` rows, CTA at the bottom.
    
    **`pricing-card-featured`** — the polarity-flipped "Pro" tier card.
    - Background `{tokens.color.primary}`, text `{tokens.color.on-primary}`, same shape + padding as `pricing-card`. CTA inverts to `button-secondary-sm` (white pill on black card).
    
    ### Inputs & Forms
    
    **`form-input`** — the canonical text input.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, text `{tokens.color.ink}`, 1 px solid `{tokens.color.hairline}` border, body in `{tokens.typography.body-sm}` (14 px), padding `0px {tokens.spacing.sm}`, height 40 px (the brand's `--geist-form-height`), shape `{tokens.radius.sm}` 6 px.
    
    **`form-input-sm`** — small-height variant (32 px tall) for tight forms.
    - Same as `form-input` but height 32 px (the `--geist-form-small-height`).
    
    **`form-input-lg`** — large-height variant (48 px tall) for hero CTAs.
    - Same as `form-input` but height 48 px (the `--geist-form-large-height`); body in `{tokens.typography.body-md}` 16 px.
    
    ### Navigation
    
    **`nav-bar`** — the sticky top nav.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, text `{tokens.color.ink}`, height 64 px (the brand's `--header-height`), padding `{tokens.spacing.sm} {tokens.spacing.lg}`. Layout: logo left, link row centre, "Ask AI / Log In / Sign Up" cluster right.
    
    **`nav-link`** — the centred link row inside `nav-bar`.
    - Text `{tokens.color.body}`, set in `{tokens.typography.body-sm}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.xs} {tokens.spacing.sm}`, shape `{tokens.radius.full}` (ghost pill — visible only on hover or active, but the radius is documented).
    
    **`footer`** — the bottom 4-column nav.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, text `{tokens.color.body}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.4xl} {tokens.spacing.lg}`. Eyebrow column labels in `{tokens.typography.caption-mono}` (uppercase mono effect); link rows in `{tokens.typography.body-sm}`.
    
    ### Signature Components
    
    **`hero-band`** — the white hero with the mesh gradient backdrop.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}` (or `{tokens.color.canvas-soft}` on some surfaces), text `{tokens.color.ink}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.4xl} {tokens.spacing.lg}`. Inside: a small mono badge above the headline, the headline in `{tokens.typography.display-xl}` (sentence-case, period-terminated), a body lead in `{tokens.typography.body-lg}`, then a CTA row with `button-primary` + `button-secondary`. The mesh gradient sits behind, scaled to occupy roughly the top half of the band.
    
    **`feature-mesh-band`** — the secondary section that hosts a mesh-gradient atmospheric backdrop with feature copy on top.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, text `{tokens.color.ink}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.5xl} {tokens.spacing.lg}`. Section headline in `{tokens.typography.display-lg}`; supporting body in `{tokens.typography.body-md}`.
    
    **`showcase-band-light`** — a soft-canvas section ("Deploy your first app in seconds").
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas-soft}`, text `{tokens.color.ink}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.5xl} {tokens.spacing.lg}`.
    
    **`showcase-band-dark`** — the polarity-flipped dark band ("A compute model for all workloads").
    - Background `{tokens.color.primary}`, text `{tokens.color.on-primary}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.5xl} {tokens.spacing.lg}`. Section headline in `{tokens.typography.display-lg}` (white on black). Often contains a `code-editor-mockup` flush with the band.
    
    **`logo-strip`** — the customer-logo wrapping row near the top of the page.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, text `{tokens.color.body}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.lg} {tokens.spacing.xl}`. Logos rendered as monochrome SVGs at consistent height.
    
    **`badge-secondary`** — the small inline metadata pill ("New", "Beta", "Live").
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas-soft}`, text `{tokens.color.body}`, body in `{tokens.typography.caption}`, padding `0px {tokens.spacing.xs}`, shape `{tokens.radius.full}`.
    
    **`banner-marketing`** — the "Introducing X" announcement pill at the top of pages.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas-soft}`, text `{tokens.color.body}`, body in `{tokens.typography.body-sm}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.xs} {tokens.spacing.sm}`, shape `{tokens.radius.full}`.
    
    **`link-inline`** — body-copy inline links.
    - Text `{tokens.color.link}` (`#0070f3`), body in `{tokens.typography.body-md}`, underlined.
    
    ### Examples (illustrative)
    
    > Auto-derived kit-mirror demonstration surfaces (`scripts/derive-examples-block.mjs`). Each `ex-*` entry references brand-native primitives so downstream consumers (`/preview-design`, `/generate-kit`) re-skin the same 10 surfaces consistently. `TO_FILL` markers indicate missing primitives — resolve in the LLM judgment pass.
    
    **`ex-pricing-tier`** — Default Pricing tier card. Re-uses feature-card chrome with brand canvas-soft surface.
    - Properties: `backgroundColor`, `textColor`, `borderColor`, `rounded`, `padding`
    
    **`ex-pricing-tier-featured`** — Featured/highlighted tier — polarity-flipped surface (dark fill + light text in light mode, light fill + dark text in dark mode).
    - Properties: `backgroundColor`, `textColor`, `rounded`, `padding`
    
    **`ex-product-selector`** — What's Included summary card — re-purposed for SaaS / B2B verticals (NOT a literal product gallery).
    - Properties: `backgroundColor`, `rounded`, `padding`
    
    **`ex-cart-drawer`** — Subscription summary — re-purposed for SaaS / B2B (line items per add-on, not literal cart).
    - Properties: `backgroundColor`, `rounded`, `padding`, `item-divider`
    
    **`ex-app-shell-row`** — Sidebar nav row inside the App Shell example. Active state uses brand primary as the indicator.
    - Properties: `backgroundColor`, `activeIndicator`, `rounded`, `padding`
    
    **`ex-data-table-cell`** — Default data-table th + td chrome. Header uses mono-caps eyebrow typography; body uses body-sm.
    - Properties: `headerBackground`, `headerTypography`, `bodyTypography`, `cellPadding`, `rowBorder`
    
    **`ex-auth-form-card`** — Sign-in / sign-up card. Re-uses feature-card chrome with text-input primitives inside.
    - Properties: `backgroundColor`, `rounded`, `padding`
    
    **`ex-modal-card`** — Modal dialog surface — same chrome as feature-card with elevated shadow.
    - Properties: `backgroundColor`, `rounded`, `padding`
    
    **`ex-empty-state-card`** — Empty-state illustration frame.
    - Properties: `backgroundColor`, `rounded`, `padding`, `captionTypography`
    
    **`ex-toast`** — Toast notification surface — feature-card shape + medium shadow.
    - Properties: `backgroundColor`, `rounded`, `padding`, `typography`
  dos:
    - "Reserve `{tokens.color.primary}` (`#171717`) for primary CTAs across the page. Black ink IS the conversion target."
    - "Use `{tokens.radius.pill}` 100 px for every marketing-scale CTA and `{tokens.radius.sm}` 6 px for nav-scale buttons. The two pill scales coexist deliberately."
    - "Set every headline in `{tokens.typography.display-*}` weight 600, sentence-case, often period-terminated. Aggressive negative tracking is part of the voice."
    - "Use the brand mesh gradient as atmospheric decoration at hero scale only \u2014 never miniaturise it to an icon, never reduce to a single colour."
    - Layer stacked shadows (multiple small offsets with inset hairline) rather than single heavy drops. The brand's elevation is calmer than Material.
    - "Cycle page surfaces in `{tokens.color.canvas-soft}` \u2192 `{tokens.color.canvas}` \u2192 `{tokens.color.primary}` polarity-flipped bands; the dark band IS the depth cue."
    - "Set every code block and technical eyebrow in `{tokens.typography.code}` / `{tokens.typography.caption-mono}`. Mono is the voice of the platform."
  donts:
    - introduce a sixth accent colour. The brand operates with ink + gray + the four-pair gradient palette; new accents flatten the voice.
    - render headlines in all-caps. Sentence-case + negative tracking is non-negotiable.
    - drop a single heavy drop-shadow on cards. The brand's elevation is built from stacked small offsets + inset hairline rings.
    - render the brand gradient at icon scale or in a single-colour reduced form. The gradient lives at hero scale only.
    - promote the geometric sans to weight 700. The brand's display ceiling is 600.
    - pair the marketing 100-px pill CTA shape with the 6-px nav radius on the same screen — pick a scale and stay there.
    - set body paragraphs in the mono face. The mono is for code + technical labels only.

omitted:
  - section: tokens.elevation
    reason: "Depth model lives in rationale.elevation; add shadow tokens as they stabilize"

integrations:
  shadcn:
    enabled: true
    style: new-york
    css_variables: true
    base_color: neutral
    css: app/globals.css
    components_json: ./components.json
    aliases:
      components: "@/components"
      utils: "@/lib/utils"
      ui: "@/components/ui"
    radius: "8px"
    css_vars:
      light:
        background: "#ffffff"
        foreground: "#171717"
        card: "#ffffff"
        card-foreground: "#171717"
        popover: "#ffffff"
        popover-foreground: "#171717"
        primary: "#171717"
        primary-foreground: "#ffffff"
        secondary: "#f4f4f5"
        secondary-foreground: "#171717"
        muted: "#f4f4f5"
        muted-foreground: "#888888"
        accent: "#f4f4f5"
        accent-foreground: "#171717"
        destructive: "#ee0000"
        border: "#ebebeb"
        input: "#ebebeb"
        ring: "#171717"
    map_from_tokens:
      background: tokens.color.canvas|tokens.color.surface|tokens.color.background
      foreground: tokens.color.ink|tokens.color.text|tokens.color.foreground
      primary: tokens.color.primary
      primary-foreground: tokens.color.on-primary
      border: tokens.color.hairline|tokens.color.border
      ring: tokens.color.primary-focus|tokens.color.primary

policy:
  if_missing: ask
  hierarchy: [typography, spacing, contrast, color]
  reuse:
    prefer_existing_components: true
  accessibility:
    contrast: AA
    focus_visible: required

constraints:
  always:
    - use semantic tokens from this file; never invent off-brand hex
    - bind every listed component property (backgroundColor, textColor, typography, rounded, padding, size, height, width)
    - read rationale.layout / rationale.elevation / rationale.shapes before inventing chrome
    - when shadcn is enabled, apply integrations.shadcn.css_vars to globals.css
    - prefer catalog components over one-off controls
    - "Reserve `{tokens.color.primary}` (`#171717`) for primary CTAs across the page. Black ink IS the conversion target."
    - "Use `{tokens.radius.pill}` 100 px for every marketing-scale CTA and `{tokens.radius.sm}` 6 px for nav-scale buttons. The two pill scales coexist deliberately."
    - "Set every headline in `{tokens.typography.display-*}` weight 600, sentence-case, often period-terminated. Aggressive negative tracking is part of the voice."
    - "Use the brand mesh gradient as atmospheric decoration at hero scale only \u2014 never miniaturise it to an icon, never reduce to a single colour."
    - Layer stacked shadows (multiple small offsets with inset hairline) rather than single heavy drops. The brand's elevation is calmer than Material.
    - "Cycle page surfaces in `{tokens.color.canvas-soft}` \u2192 `{tokens.color.canvas}` \u2192 `{tokens.color.primary}` polarity-flipped bands; the dark band IS the depth cue."
    - "Set every code block and technical eyebrow in `{tokens.typography.code}` / `{tokens.typography.caption-mono}`. Mono is the voice of the platform."
  never:
    - generic purple-on-white AI chrome unrelated to this brand
    - dropping DESIGN.md component variants or rationale during restyle
    - introduce a sixth accent colour. The brand operates with ink + gray + the four-pair gradient palette; new accents flatten the voice.
    - render headlines in all-caps. Sentence-case + negative tracking is non-negotiable.
    - drop a single heavy drop-shadow on cards. The brand's elevation is built from stacked small offsets + inset hairline rings.
    - render the brand gradient at icon scale or in a single-colour reduced form. The gradient lives at hero scale only.
    - promote the geometric sans to weight 700. The brand's display ceiling is 600.
    - pair the marketing 100-px pill CTA shape with the 6-px nav radius on the same screen — pick a scale and stay there.
    - set body paragraphs in the mono face. The mono is for code + technical labels only.

